From 108b74aaf488177cea882b87bb0ef3dabf97f8b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:54:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(engine): evaluate T of S \subseteq T before testing
 S's elements in it

Tool's OPCODE_subseteq evaluates both operands, then tests each element
of S in T. Where T is a set the engine tests without building, it ran
T's member test only per element of S, so with S empty it never made
the tests TLC makes as it builds T, such as the reduction of
BOOLEAN \ [SUBSET Nat -> ...], which fails, and answered TRUE. It now
runs T's parts first, and declines where a test runs them again with
effects. One run of the upstream conformance suite that printed FALSE
where TLC fails now declines.
